    "title": "22-Year-Old Killed In Chain-Reaction Crash On Garden State Parkway In Woodbridge - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Cecilia Levine ,\n5 hours ago New Jersey State Police (NJSP) Photo Credit: New Jersey State Police (NJSP) Li Wei Lin was driving a Honda passenger car on the Garden State Parkway entrance ramp from Route 27 when the vehicle ran off the right side of the road and struck a guardrail at approximately 2:15 p.m. at milepost 132.2, according to State Police Sgt. Charles Marchan.\nAfter hitting the guardrail, the Honda continued on the ramp and entered the northbound lanes of the Parkway, perpendicular to the flow of traffic, police said.\nA 57-year-old woman from Barnegat was driving a Lexus SUV northbound on the Parkway when the vehicle struck the Honda, police said. After that impact, the Honda struck a concrete barrier, according to state police.\nPolice said a 74-year-old man from Beach Haven, driving a Ram pickup truck northbound on the Parkway, then struck the Lexus from behind.\nLin died as a result of the crash, police said. The 57-year-old woman was not injured, and the 74-year-old man sustained minor injuries, according to state police.\nThe crash remains under investigation, and no additional information is available, police said.\nto follow Daily Voice Woodbridge and receive free news updates.\n1",
